WEBVTT

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.000
Now, go.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.860
Do your work for me.

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:14.830
A hospital again?

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.490
Oh, looks like you're awake.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.000
Doctor, am I...

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:29.340
It is truly unfortunate,

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.000
but both had to be removed completely.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.710
So I can find out how

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:56.030
to get back to my world 
by going to the capital?

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.720
Were you even listening to what I said?

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.050
I said there's a possibility.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.760
Still, there's a possibility, right?

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:04.580
Yeah.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.580
The light that we saw when 
you used that weapon...

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.620
That was definitely the 
glow of Alma Energy.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.670
And remember how you 
first fell from the sky?

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.200
You might have come from Olvidia.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.130
Ol...?

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.600
Olvidia, the legendary continent

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.070
that was lifted into the 
skies by the Ixions

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.890
a long time ago.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.390
Ah yeah, the castle in the 
sky. I know that one.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.400
It's destroyed when you 
say "Bals!" right?

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.940
I don't know if Bals would break it,

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.830
but there's a deep connection between

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.460
the Ixions and Alma Crystals.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.260
So those people were the first

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.090
to start using the Alma Crystals, huh?

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:50.540
How did you know? 
You're right, but...

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.970
I just had a feeling that 
it would be like that.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:55.040
It's common.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.040
Oh.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.630
You're so cute!

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:13.770
Oh no, it's so cute!

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.790
It's rare for a wild animal 
to get so close to people.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.530
It's a pretty stupid animal if it's

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.030
looking up at Kon instead of me.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.370
All right, guys, we're in 
the middle of our journey.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:33.660
Let's keep moving!

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:35.640
But...

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.400
Listen, sis, we have been entrusted with

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.550
the mission to reach the 
capital as soon as possible.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.960
We don't have time to deal 
with this kind of critter.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.800
But we can't just leave this little—

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.260
That's the kind of half-hearted

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.180
humanism that ruins wild animals!

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.880
Why don't you understand that 
that kind of irresponsible,

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.690
fleeting kindness ultimately 
breeds tragedy?!

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:03.960
But maybe this one's hungry.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.770
And after that?

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:07.810
Do you intend to take 
care of it until it dies?

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.640
Well...

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:14.150
In the animal kingdom, 
as always described by the

00:05:14.150 --> 00:05:16.710
special animal channels 
and animal documentaries...

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.210
Yes!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.260
It's the harshness of the wilderness!

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.680
The law of the jungle!

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.860
Survival of the fittest!

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.510
A bear that was abandoned by 
its parents because it was too weak!

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.590
A seal that was 
relaxing on the beach

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:30.220
is suddenly eaten by an orca!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.250
The weak will be eaten!

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.730
That's the law of the wilderness!

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.480
I have no idea what 
you're talking about!

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:42.360
What are you getting so heated for?

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.160
I'm trying to say just one thing.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:48.330
Don't get involved with this creature!

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.120
Go away!

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.760
Go back to the wilderness!

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.630
What are you doing?!

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.630
You were mistaken if you 
thought that getting

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:04.630
all cuddly with humans 
would get you something.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:09.410
It's best for it to live on 
its own in the wilderness.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.140
Let's go.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.650
Did you hear about Erec-sama?

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.660
I heard he's going to take a leave 
from his position for a while.

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:34.660
That's no surprise, 
considering what happened.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.080
There are a lot of rumors going around.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.440
Some say he's going on a 
medical leave for a while,

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.330
others say he was forced 
to take responsibility

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.820
for losing a Chariot.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.510
I'm worried.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.920
He was beaten twice 
by the same opponent.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:52.640
So the psychological damage is 
greater than the physical damage.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.640
All we can do is believe 
in him and wait.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:04.210
That's the current mission of our 
special brigade, Incognito.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.400
I wonder what's going on.

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:12.910
Why did he get so worked up?

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:14.910
It was cute.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.590
Not sure, but it looked 
like he did have a reason.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:21.920
Though I doubt he would 
answer if we asked him.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.880
I wonder what it's doing now.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.930
Oh well, no use worrying about it.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.890
Time to sleep. 
I hope I have a nice dream.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.530
Can't breathe...

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.120
I was supposed to have a nice dream.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.630
Why am I being tortured 
by such a heavy nightmare?

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:10.550
What happened?!

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.900
Oh, you followed us all the way here.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.270
Why aren't you more concerned?!

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.060
Take that thing out already!

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.470
Now I know why I had 
that heavy nightmare.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:26.810
Why don't you take it?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.320
This is my room!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.340
It must have taken 
such a liking to you

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.320
that it followed you into your room.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.820
I didn't ask for this!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:37.830
Well, being liked by an animal 
isn't anything to brag about.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.680
If this looks like bragging to you,

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:41.830
you must be really stupid!

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.830
Sainglain, what do you think?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.830
Well, I think its cu—

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:49.090
This is bad!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.340
This thing is bad!

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.640
It's a mysterious little critter!

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:54.540
What are you talking about?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.500
I don't care if you believe me or not,

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.250
but please, just take it out!

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.320
There's no need for that.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.240
Come here, little one.

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:10.130
Hey, sis...

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.570
I'll take responsibility.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.280
I will take care of this little creature.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.370
Totally out of the question!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.990
I will not have it!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.870
Why are you talking like a mother?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.790
Let me warn you.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.410
Pets are only cute in the beginning.

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.930
They get big quickly and then

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.880
you don't know what to do with them.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.380
I'm not saying this out of malice.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:36.190
Take it back to where

00:09:36.190 --> 00:09:38.440
we found it before you get too attached.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:39.460
No!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.700
I told you that I won't have it!

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:45.130
And you know, you're always like this!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.650
The turtle, the goldfish, the chick,

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.990
in the end it was always your 
mother who took care of them!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.900
Again, why are you 
talking like a mother?

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.400
I don't care what you say, 
my mind is made up.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:59.890
Don't you worry, 
I'll take care of you.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:04.660
Why do you lower your voice for that?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.210
Are you done now?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.670
No, not yet.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:12.310
I didn't think I'd have to say this,

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:15.670
but it looks like I'll have to do it.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.160
Hey, sis.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.950
Isn't your most important mission,

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.680
that is, protecting the princess, 
going to be affected by

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.350
you being infatuated with that animal?

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.440
That's...

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.540
We are the princess's servants,

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.290
I don't think I have to spell out 
what the most important thing is.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:36.660
In the past, there was a 
great hero called Arthur.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:41.260
He was a true master with the sword,

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:46.000
and he had an absolutely 
brilliant mind, as well.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.830
Using his sword and tactics so novel

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.070
they could be called tricks,

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:53.090
he survived countless deadly encounters

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.960
and saved many of his comrades.

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:59.970
As much as his allies relied on 
him as the Fang of St. Piria,

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.280
his enemies feared him.

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:06.270
It is said that Arthur, 
survivor of myriad battles,

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.730
one day uttered:

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.290
"I really like cats."

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:15.980
The hell is that?!

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:18.240
When I remembered that,

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.870
I realized that we can't 
even begin trying to

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:25.290
protect the princess's safety if 
we can't protect this little life.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.750
You're so cute!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.060
You just love pets!

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:34.860
And did we really need that story?

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.750
And what's with the muscle 
freak loving pets?

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:39.430
Aren't you trying too hard to 
make your character interesting?

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:41.760
Two versus one.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.980
Wait, I'm not done...

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:45.060
Shut up already.

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:47.300
I've had enough of your whining.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.020
The discussion is over.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.520
What now?

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.520
Anyway, that thing's dangerous!

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.700
I'm telling you, it's like shacking 
up with an unknown monster,

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.940
so don't do it!

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.610
Don't take it personally.

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.350
It might surprise you, but I do 
not dislike rewarding my servants.

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:06.790
Oh yeah? Well then I've 
got an idea, too.

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:19.670
<i>Beast, I'm sorry, but I'm</i>

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.420
<i>an amazing hunter with 
a Hunter Rank of 161.</i>

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:26.970
<i>I know all about the hunt.</i>

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.530
Excuse me.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:29.790
Welcome!

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:32.480
I'd like some tinged meat 
and a pitfall trap.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.730
Oh, and a barrel bomb and...

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.980
What are you doing?

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.480
Uh, just preparing for hunting.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.240
<i>Beast, my Hunter Rank is 161.</i>

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:55.500
<i>My skill with the Mega 
Bug Net is unrivaled.</i>

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:02.350
I'll slam you into the 
bottom of an Item Box!

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.000
What are you doing?

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:08.350
Uh, just gathering some supplies.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:12.260
<i>I'm an amazing hunter.</i>

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:16.290
<i>I have memorized all the recipes.</i>

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:20.640
I'll have you afflicted with Garo

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.390
and Adrenaline at the same time!

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:23.480
What are you doing?

00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:27.780
Uh, I was just cooking a little.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.540
I see, you eat it first, then.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.350
Well, that's...

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.920
So, I've been getting reports

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:45.030
that you've been acting suspiciously,

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:46.930
and I've seen it myself.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.680
Please explain yourself.

00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.190
What am I supposed to explain?

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.430
Why do you hate this guy?

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:59.980
Originally it followed us because 
it took a liking to you.

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:01.780
Isn't that right?

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:06.670
A knight is required to not only 
be skilled with the sword,

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.860
he also needs to be 
noble and well mannered.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:10.700
And on top of that...

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.700
I can't fathom why

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:16.040
anyone could hate such 
a cute little being!

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:25.250
All right, I give up. I'll tell you

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.080
the truth about myself.

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.850
I actually have a pet allergy.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.830
Pet allergy?

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.340
Allergy?

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:37.350
What's that?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.850
Simply put, I don't feel good

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:43.380
when that thing gets near me.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.860
But that's...

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.610
I see, I understand now.

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.290
But you seem fine despite that.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:15:00.090
Who gave you permission 
to get on my head?!

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.990
Damn you!

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.380
Damn you!

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.750
You stupid animal!

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:06.150
Ow!

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:08.260
So you were lying.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.760
What is it with you?!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.010
Do you understand what we're saying?

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.370
I feel like you're messing with me!

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.770
You're the one messing 
with us, you idiot!

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.110
Enough of your foolishness.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.060
This matter is now cl—

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.600
Please wait, princess.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.660
You must have a reason.

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:35.410
I can't believe that you'd 
do something like this

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.320
without one.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.790
Ah yes, I believe it was 
a full moon that night

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.660
and the crabs in the 
buckets were really noisy...

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:45.250
Be serious.

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:55.120
This was back when I was still a kid.

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:58.810
I was caught in a sudden downpour

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:01.440
and I was getting soaked

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:04.060
trying to get home quickly on my bike.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:09.070
When I was passing in 
front of a thicket,

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:12.570
I heard a faint noise from it.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:16.410
The noise was really faint and was

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.220
almost completely muffled 
by the sound of the rain.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:23.580
Thinking back, I don't 
know how I noticed it.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:28.090
But back then I definitely heard it.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.750
I felt like it was fate.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:36.140
That I had to save those two lives.

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:38.480
I mean it's true, right?

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.350
You can't just pretend 
you didn't see anything

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.570
when you hear those desperate cries.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:48.360
That's why I took the 
two cats back home.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.670
I desperately tried to 
convince my mother and

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:54.360
got permission to bring the 
two cats into our house.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:16:59.850
But...

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:05.350
What happened?!

00:17:05.700 --> 00:17:08.880
Were you traumatized because 
someone in your family objected

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.610
to having them and told 
you to put them out again?

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:13.110
No.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.580
Don't tell me...

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:19.390
Don't tell me something 
happened to those two!

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:21.530
No, that's not it either.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:26.900
Then what happened?

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.990
Thanks to my desperate pleas,

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.830
those two were allowed 
to enter our household.

00:17:34.940 --> 00:17:36.910
They had overly healthy appetites and

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.260
grew bigger and bigger 
without getting sick.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.910
So what was the problem?

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:45.250
There were a ton of problems.

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.830
I looked after them as 
much as time permitted.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:50.200
And still...

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.340
And still...

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:57.640
Those two never liked 
me for some reason!

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.430
How dare they do that

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:02.040
to the one who saved their lives?!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:04.310
What?

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.410
Since that time I've sworn

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:11.820
that I'll never get involved 
with cute animals ever again!

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:18.500
Well, so, in times like these,

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:21.580
are we supposed to 
offer our condolences?

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:26.320
By the way, they are still 
happily part of my family!

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.930
That's no reason to 
be mean to this guy.

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:33.080
She's right.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:34.740
Kon, you were wrong.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.310
But this is a chance.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:41.720
A chance to correct your mistake.

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:43.870
My mistake?

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:45.540
That's right.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.260
You still have time. 
If you're willing, that is.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.480
Open your heart.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.720
Then I'm sure it'll respond.

00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.780
My heart...

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:07.220
<i>If you feel that it's 
cute, then I'm sure...</i>

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:12.140
I'm sorry for what I did, beast.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:16.090
I... I was wron—

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.430
Ow!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.070
Let go, you! Ow!

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:25.010
Damn you! Damn you! Damn you!

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:34.610
You little...

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:35.970
I will not

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.830
forgive

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:38.990
you!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.260
Easy now.

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:44.490
That's way over the top 
for such a small animal.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:47.150
You guys stay out of this.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:50.690
This is a fight between men, him and me.

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:52.740
Is it really that kind of problem?

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:56.000
We don't even know if 
it's a boy or a girl.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.630
Shut up, stay out of this!

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.760
Hey, beast! This is a fight 
between you and me!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.330
If I win, you'll get out of my sight!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:10.200
If you win, don't ever show 
yourself in front of me either!

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:12.390
That's not right.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.900
You should at least make 
a compromise if you lose.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:19.900
Shut up! Like I'd lose to this thing!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:24.740
All right, fine, if I lose, 
I'll do whatever you want.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:27.880
Sainglain!

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:28.410
Yes!

00:20:28.730 --> 00:20:30.910
Surge, my Alma!

00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:30.870
Kon!

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:35.210
Oh no!

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:47.220
Not bad...

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.270
I won't hold back anymore!

00:20:51.090 --> 00:20:52.480
Die, die!

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.900
Die, die!

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.100
Hold back?

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.610
He was serious, 
definitely dead serious.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.240
Kon, enough already!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.530
Shut up and watch!

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:07.490
Ow!

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.630
I'll kick your ass!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.880
You fell for it!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.470
This is it!

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.400
It's over.

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:59.170
Well, everything got settled 
nicely in the end, right?

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:02.000
Nicely? Everything's crap.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:06.580
Being a sore loser is a 
disgrace for a knight.

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:12.700
We got a new friend. 
We should all be happy, right?

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:19.550
I won't forget this.

00:22:19.550 --> 00:22:22.430
I'll eat you one of these days!

00:22:27.310 --> 00:22:29.330
Erec-sama!

00:22:30.430 --> 00:22:32.770
Where are you going?

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:34.040
Variation?

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:36.270
You need a ride, right?

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:24.850
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:10.730 --> 00:24:12.910
After being wounded in 
my battle against DT,

00:24:12.910 --> 00:24:15.760
I returned to my 
hometown for some rest.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:18.310
There, an old friend 
was waiting for me.

00:24:18.310 --> 00:24:20.810
And an evil conspiracy...

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:24.850
I, Erecpyle Dukakis, 
accept your challenge!

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:29.860
Emilia, his pure and innocent fiancée,

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:29.860
was waiting for Erec.

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:35.040
As well as the two siblings Limpus and Gabriella,

00:24:29.860 --> 00:24:35.040
who are plotting against Erec.
